Stress Testing
Stress Testing is an integral part of the Liquidity Risk Management Framework. The objective of stress testing is to 
ensure that the Bank maintains adequate level of liquidity to be able to withstand a range of severe stress scenario. 
The Bank conducts liquidity stress testing across Systemic, Bank Specific and Combined Scenarios and ensures 
that the Survival Horizon across these stress scenarios remains within the Board approved appetite. The Stress 
Tests are conducted on a periodic basis and updated to the Group ALCO and the BRC.

